At Vandana, your trust matters to us. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, why we use it, and the choices available to you.
1. About this policy
This Privacy Policy applies to the Vandana mobile application, website, and related services (collectively, the “Service”). By using the Service, you acknowledge the practices described here.
2. Information we collect
Depending on how you use Vandana, we may collect:
- Account information, such as your name, email address, phone number, or profile details when you create an account.
- Content you provide, including information, messages, files, or preferences you choose to add to the Service.
- Usage and device information, such as app interactions, device type, operating system, app version, IP address, and diagnostic data.
- Support communications when you contact us for help or feedback.
3. How we use information
We use information to operate, secure, and improve Vandana. This includes providing requested features, personalising your experience, responding to support requests, detecting fraud or misuse, and communicating important service updates.
4. When we share information
We may share information with trusted providers that help us run the Service, such as hosting, analytics, customer support, and payment providers. They may only use information to perform services for us.

We may also disclose information when required by law, to protect rights and safety, or as part of a business transfer. We do not sell personal information.
5. Data retention
We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including legal, accounting, and security requirements. We may retain de-identified or aggregated information for longer.
6. Your choices and rights
You can update certain account details through the app. Subject to applicable law, you may request access to, correction of, deletion of, or a copy of your personal information.

You may also opt out of non-essential marketing messages by following the unsubscribe instructions in those messages.
7. Security
We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organisational safeguards designed to protect your information. However, no online service can guarantee absolute security.
8. Children’s privacy
Vandana is not directed to children under the age at which parental consent is required in their country. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without appropriate consent. If you believe a child has provided us information, please contact us.
9. Changes to this policy
We may update this policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we will provide notice through the Service or by other appropriate means. The effective date above shows when this policy was last revised.
